{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/816459-pyretics-level-1-and-2-how-to-make-use-of-them","id":816459,"title":"Pyretics level 1 and 2 how to make use of them.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-25T15:19:14-08:00","id":816459,"title":"Pyretics level 1 and 2 how to make use of them.","content":"Pyretics is one of the most obvious arts for a PC who wants flashy and violent power...<br /> <br /> the ironic thing, is the first 2 dots are the ones that require the most brains to use... at least in how to incorporate them into an NPC Villains strategy. and when imagining &quot;What did he do with these, while he was training&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 01-25-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:16:15-08:00","id":816585,"title":"","content":"Can you be more specific? They seem pretty self-explanatory to me:<br /> <br /> 'This cantrip creates a ball of chimerical flame that will lead its creator to a specific place, person or object. This cantrip is often used as the &quot;lead dog&quot; in a hunt.'<br /> <br /> 'This cantrip will allow you to illuminate or cast auras of light upon objects or places. With this cantrip you can cause objects or people to glow, or even cause an entire place to become lit by this phosphorescence.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 01-26-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:52:17-08:00","id":816610,"title":"","content":"Anything that an NPC Villain with them can do beyond one or two niceh situations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:14:19-08:00","id":816852,"title":"","content":"The NPC villain is a nigh-infallible tracker. Whether he overtly has the ball of flame lead him to his quarry, or he covertly sneaks up on them so he can keep following them and pop out at a dramatic moment, there's no AVOIDING him. You also cannot hide anything from him; if he wants an object, he WILL find it. Using this to gather items of power or blackmail materials could both be useful.<br /> <br /> He can also foil others' stealth when he is around and aware of them, causing light to draw the eye to those people he wants revealed. Not to mention his own dramatic lighting effects. Light up an area brighter than normal, except where you want to hide, and you can improve your own stealth capabilities. And, of course, making a mundane item glow can be helpful in selling a &quot;magic&quot; tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:16:47-08:00","id":817157,"title":"","content":"Well it's simple, really: just try the Arts with different Realms.<br /> <br /> With Nature, you can find a tree, a particular bee, maybe even the Higgs boson.<br /> <br /> With Fae, you can find a changeling, chimera, or a particular spell or ward.<br /> <br /> With Actor, you can find an enemy, a celebrity, an expert who knows everything about a specific subject.<br /> <br /> With Prop, you can find a lost item, a pile of cash or even the Triumph Casque of Sorrows.<br /> <br /> Say you want to kill your enemy, you can use Pyretics 1 to find a hitman, or even just a person who is homicidal enough that you might be able to convince them to kill your enemy for free.<br /> <br /> Pyretics 2 can be used to scare off vampires, light up a mine, create light in a midnight street. Really this power is less useful than Pyretics 1, IMO, so they should be swapped around, but it's still useful enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}